nswer.type/math "{\\int }_{2}^{4}\\sqrt{1+4x}\\,\\text{d}x"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010575/state.json" "file_sha256" "f4385d0f6702ca6f8197ed3cc32c7f1c79cd2ae6f62bf5f1f7e599e97c1288a7" "basis" 1147 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010575/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-5984" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "{\\int }_{2}^{4}\\sqrt{1+\\frac{2}{3}{x}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010575/state.json" "file_sha256" "f4385d0f6702ca6f8197ed3cc32c7f1c79cd2ae6f62bf5f1f7e599e97c1288a7" "basis" 1147 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010575/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-5984" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{\\int }_{2}^{4}\\sqrt{1+16{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010575/state.json" "file_sha256" "f4385d0f6702ca6f8197ed3cc32c7f1c79cd2ae6f62bf5f1f7e599e97c1288a7" "basis" 1147 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010575/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-15327" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010575/assets/431975da27fb1ff06baa520ef4f870cb34c879f384bfc5ddd774422f15fe7b57.png)\n\nWhich of the following gives the length of the curve $y=4{e}^{-{x}^{2}/4}$ on $[0,2],$ as shown above?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010575/state.json" "file_sha256" "f4385d0f6702ca6f8197ed3cc32c7f1c79cd2ae6f62bf5f1f7e599e97c1288a7" "basis" 1147 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010575/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-15327" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The arc length of a curve $y=f(x)$ between $x=a$ and $x=b$ can be found using the formula\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{a}^{b}\\sqrt{1+[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $f(x)=4{e}^{-{x}^{2}/4},$ $a=0,$ and $b=2.$\n\nFirst, we find the derivative of $f(x):$\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=4(\\frac{-2x}{4}){e}^{-{x}^{2}/4}=-2x{e}^{-{x}^{2}/4}\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${f}^{′}(x)=-2x{e}^{-{x}^{2}/4}$ into the arc length formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}\\sqrt{1+{[{f}^{′}(x)]}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}\\sqrt{1+{(-2x{e}^{-{x}^{2}/4})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}\\sqrt{1+4{x}^{2}{e}^{-{x}^{2}/2}}\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010575/state.json" "file_sha256" "f4385d0f6702ca6f8197ed3cc32c7f1c79cd2ae6f62bf5f1f7e599e97c1288a7" "basis" 1147 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010575/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-15327" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010575/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4e4b183965c62a7c75bfaa462ee8efd70fbadef48beebfed1b114ec3ed6029cf" "basis" 1147 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010575/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-15327" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010575/state.json" "file_sha256" "f4385d0f6702ca6f8197ed3cc32c7